================================================================================
Scope of this file
================================================================================

This is an attribution aid, not legal advice, and not a warranty that the list
is exhaustive: transitive dependencies of the packages above bring in further
components. Generate a full inventory from a built image if you need one, for
example with `docker sbom` or `syft`, which is also what the `buildx` targets in
the Makefile attach as an SBOM.

The engines with copyleft components are called out above rather than buried:
Pandoc (GPL) in the five Pandoc-based engines, Ghostscript (AGPL) in ocr, and
PyMuPDF (AGPL or commercial) in pii and pdf2docx. The two engines with no
copyleft component at all are convert2md and liteparse, whose bundled software
is MIT, Apache-2.0, MPL-2.0 and BSD-3-Clause.
